#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Change a system setting for the Settings window (flickos-control).

Runs as root through pkexec; polkit asks for an administrator's password
(/usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.flickos.control.policy, one action per verb).
Only these verbs exist, and every value is checked before anything changes:

  keyboard MODEL LAYOUT VARIANT OPTIONS
      The keyboard of the login screen, the console and new accounts:
      /etc/default/keyboard (keyboard-configuration; keyboard(5)). Each value
      must be in the XKB rules list (evdev.lst); several layouts, variants and
      options are separated by commas. The file's other lines are kept. The
      login screen uses it at its next start, the console at the next boot.

  autologin-on
      Log the calling user (pkexec's PKEXEC_UID, a regular account) in
      without a password once per boot: that user becomes the only member of
      group autologin, whose first member flickos-greeter logs in.

  autologin-off
      The calling user leaves group autologin.

  user-add NAME FULLNAME ADMIN
      Add a regular account (adduser, so /etc/skel is copied) with the
      password on standard input, in the groups the installer gives the first
      account (DEFAULT_GROUPS), and in group sudo if ADMIN is "yes".

  user-remove NAME FILES
      Remove a regular account (userdel) that is not logged in and not the
      calling user's; FILES "delete" also deletes its home folder, "keep"
      leaves it.

  user-admin NAME ADMIN
      Put a regular account in group sudo ("yes") or take it out ("no").

  user-password NAME
      Set a regular account's password to the one on standard input.

  firewall-on
      Turn the ufw firewall on now and at every start (ufw --force enable:
      no question about ssh connections, there is nobody to answer it).

  firewall-off
      Turn the ufw firewall off now and at every start (ufw disable).

  firewall-phones on|off|refresh
      Let phones with the KDE Connect app (flickos-phone) through the
      firewall, only from private addresses (PRIVATE_NETWORKS), or stop
      letting them. on writes a ufw app profile (PHONES_PROFILE: TCP 1716
      and 1739-1764, UDP 1716 for a phone's broadcast) and allows it from
      each private range; off deletes those rules and the profile. The
      profile is there exactly while phones are let in, which is how
      flickos-control reads this setting (ufw's own rules need root even to
      read). refresh rewrites an outdated FlickOS profile and its rules
      (ufw app update) and does nothing else; flickos-control's postinst
      runs it, so an upgrade brings new ports to phones already let in.

  power SETTING ACTION
      What the power button (SETTING power-key), closing the lid (lid) or
      closing it while plugged in (lid-external-power) does: ACTION poweroff,
      suspend, lock, ignore, or default (logind's own; for the lid while
      plugged in: the same as on battery). Written to a logind drop-in
      (LOGIND_DROP_IN, its other settings kept); logind reloads it at once.

  updates SETTING VALUE | updates refresh
      Automatic updates (unattended-upgrades): SETTING auto (yes, no),
      scope (security, debian: Debian's own choice and FlickOS with its
      community apps, all: also stable-updates) or reboot (no, idle: when
      nobody is logged in); VALUE default drops the choice. Written to
      UPDATES_DROP_IN, which sorts after Debian's 20auto-upgrades and
      50unattended-upgrades. refresh writes the drop-in again from its
      stored choices with this version's origins; flickos-control's postinst
      runs it.

  firefox-memory on|off
      Make Firefox ESR use less memory, for everyone (on), or leave it to
      Firefox's own defaults (off): FIREFOX_PREFS, a file of default prefs
      that Debian's Firefox reads from /etc/firefox-esr/ at its next start.
      The prefs are fixed here (FIREFOX_MEMORY_PREFS); a user's own values
      still win. on needs Debian's firefox-esr; off works without it.

  locale-add LOCALE
      Make a language available: LOCALE must be a UTF-8 locale in
      /usr/share/i18n/SUPPORTED. Its line in /etc/locale.gen is turned on
      (or added), and locale-gen generates the locales that are missing.

  packages-undo ID
      Undo one change to the installed software (Settings > History): the
      apt transaction whose Start-Date is ID (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS), read from
      apt's own log here, never from the caller. An install is undone by
      removing the packages the user asked for, with the ones it brought in
      unless another package needs them; a removal by installing them again.
      apt simulates it first, and nothing happens if it would also remove
      another package, anything the FlickOS desktop depends on, or install a
      live-session package, or if the transaction was part of installing the
      system. Updates can't be undone (Debian keeps only the newest version).

Two verbs only read, and run without root (and without pkexec), so that the
Settings window shows the same list and plan the undo will use:

  packages-list [DAYS]
      The software changes of the last DAYS days (90) as JSON, oldest first,
      without the ones made while installing the system.

  packages-plan ID
      What packages-undo ID would do, as JSON, or why it can't.

The last administrator (member of group sudo, which polkit and sudo ask for)
can't be removed or made a standard user.

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage error.
"""

